type.description:
Set only the payload whose key equals type (text, caption and divider use text). Types:
actions: Up to 4 buttons: respond sends a reply to you; approval and entity act on the bound item. Example: {"id":"next","type":"actions","actions":[{"id":"yes","label":"Switch plan","kind":"respond","value":"Switch me to Plus"}]}
analogy: Something new explained as something familiar, with 1-5 matching pairs. Example: {"id":"like","type":"analogy","summary":"A cell works like a factory.","analogy":{"from":{"label":"Cell","icon":"dna"},"to":{"label":"Factory","icon":"building"},"mapping":[{"a":"Nucleus","b":"Head office"},{"a":"Mitochondria","b":"Power station"}]}}
before_after: A change shown side by side: two texts (diff highlights changed words, or split) or two images already in this chat (slider or split). Example: {"id":"tone","type":"before_after","summary":"The reply is warmer and asks one clear question.","before_after":{"mode":"diff","before":{"text":"Send me the report."},"after":{"text":"Could you send me the report when you have a moment?"},"labels":{"before":"Yours","after":"Suggested"}}}
callout: Key takeaway, tip or warning (markdown body); tone sets its colour, info by default. Example: {"id":"tip","type":"callout","summary":"Two streaming services go unused.","tone":"warning","callout":{"icon":"lightbulb","body":"You pay for **three** streaming services and watch one."}}
caption: Small print under a visual (sources, assumptions). Example: {"id":"src","type":"caption","text":"Prices checked today."}
carousel: 2-10 swipeable cards, e.g. recipes or places. Example: {"id":"c1","type":"carousel","children":[…]}
chart: Trend or distribution of numbers; pie and donut take one series of at most 7 slices; stacked_bar and grouped_bar need 2+ series with the same labels; scatter labels are x numbers. Example: {"id":"spend","type":"chart","summary":"Spending rose each month.","chart":{"kind":"bar","xLabel":"Month","yLabel":"Spend","format":"currency","currency":"GBP","series":[{"name":"Spend","points":[{"label":"Jan","value":120},{"label":"Feb","value":140}]}],"highlight":{"x":"Feb"}}}
checklist: 1-40 items people tick off together (packing, shopping, to-dos); you see progress next turn. Example: {"id":"pack","type":"checklist","title":"Packing list","summary":"Eight things to pack.","checklist":{"items":[{"id":"passport","label":"Passport","group":"Documents"},{"id":"charger","label":"Phone charger"}]}}
choices: 2-5 quick-reply chips under your answer; a tap answers you. Example: {"id":"next","type":"choices","summary":"Offers a shorter or a vegetarian version.","choices":{"chips":[{"id":"short","label":"Shorter"},{"id":"veg","label":"Vegetarian"}]}}
comparison: 2-4 options against the same attributes (every option gives every attribute a value); pickable lets the user pick one, which answers you. Example: {"id":"plans","type":"comparison","summary":"Sim Plus is cheapest with enough data.","comparison":{"attributes":[{"key":"data","label":"Data"}],"options":[{"id":"now","name":"Current","price":{"value":25,"format":"currency","currency":"GBP","per":"month"},"values":{"data":"60 GB"}},{"id":"plus","name":"Sim Plus","badge":"Best value","values":{"data":"30 GB"}}],"recommended":"plus","pickable":true}}
definition: One term made simple, with an optional example and image. Example: {"id":"term","type":"definition","summary":"Photosynthesis is how plants make food from light.","definition":{"term":"Photosynthesis","partOfSpeech":"noun","meaning":"How plants use sunlight, water and carbon dioxide to make sugar and oxygen.","example":"Leaves are green because of the chlorophyll photosynthesis uses."}}
diagram: How 2-30 ideas connect; pick a layout (flow, cycle, hierarchy with parent -> child edges, mindmap with the first node as centre, network) and the app places the nodes; tap a node for its detail. Example: {"id":"water","type":"diagram","summary":"Water evaporates, condenses, falls as rain and collects again.","diagram":{"layout":"cycle","nodes":[{"id":"evaporate","label":"Evaporation","icon":"sun"},{"id":"condense","label":"Condensation","icon":"cloud"},{"id":"rain","label":"Rain","icon":"droplet"}]}}
divider: Visual break, optionally labelled. Example: {"id":"d1","type":"divider"}
draft: A message you wrote for them (email, message, post or note); they can say it looks good, ask for it shorter, or edit it; bind it to the approval of a send you proposed so its buttons send or cancel. Example: {"id":"reply","type":"draft","summary":"A short, friendly reply to Sam.","draft":{"channel":"email","to":"Sam","subject":"Re: Friday","body":"Hi Sam,\n\nFriday works for me. See you at 10.\n\nAlex"}}
flashcards: A practice deck of 2-30 cards; people flip each, mark it Got it or Again, and you hear their tally when they finish. Example: {"id":"deck","type":"flashcards","title":"French food words","summary":"Five French words for food.","flashcards":{"cards":[{"id":"pain","front":"le pain","back":"bread"},{"id":"fromage","front":"le fromage","back":"cheese"}]}}
form: Structured input the user submits once. Example: {"id":"prefs","type":"form","summary":"Asks for budget and dates.","form":{"fields":[{"id":"budget","type":"number","label":"Budget","min":0}],"submitLabel":"Send"}}
gallery: 2-12 images already in this chat. Example: {"id":"rooms","type":"gallery","summary":"Three photos of the flat.","gallery":{"images":[{"image":{"artifactId":"img-1","version":1}},{"image":{"artifactId":"img-2","version":1}}],"layout":"strip"}}
grid: Children side by side in 2-4 columns. Example: {"id":"g1","type":"grid","grid":{"columns":2},"children":[…]}
image: One image already in this chat (by the id and version shown with it, never a URL) with a caption. Example: {"id":"cell","type":"image","summary":"A labelled animal cell.","image":{"image":{"artifactId":"img-1","version":1},"caption":"An animal cell"}}
item: One product, option or listing with price, rating and up to 4 facts. Example: {"id":"kettle","type":"item","summary":"A quiet 1.7 litre kettle for £35, rated 4.6.","item":{"name":"Quiet Boil kettle","price":{"value":35,"format":"currency","currency":"GBP"},"rating":{"value":4.6,"count":1200},"facts":["1.7 litres","Boils in 3 minutes"],"badge":"Quietest"}}
labeled_image: Numbered markers on an image already in this chat; x and y are 0-1 from the top-left; tap a marker for its detail. Example: {"id":"parts","type":"labeled_image","summary":"The nucleus and mitochondria of an animal cell.","labeled_image":{"image":{"artifactId":"img-1","version":1},"markers":[{"id":"nucleus","x":0.48,"y":0.5,"label":"Nucleus","detail":"Holds the DNA."},{"id":"mito","x":0.7,"y":0.3,"label":"Mitochondria"}]}}
math: A worked solution, one LaTeX line (no $ delimiters) per step with an optional note; reveal stepwise to show one step at a time. Example: {"id":"solve","type":"math","summary":"Solving 2x + 3 = 11 gives x = 4.","math":{"steps":[{"latex":"2x + 3 = 11"},{"latex":"2x = 8","note":"Take 3 from both sides"},{"latex":"x = 4","note":"Divide by 2"}],"reveal":"stepwise"}}
quantity_visual: Numbers made tangible for learners: fraction_bars (fractions), number_line (min, max, ticks, points, ranges), unit_blocks (groups), percent_waffle (parts totalling at most 100) or scale_compare (items); steps (at most 4) let people step through a change, each with the same fields. Example: {"id":"compare","type":"quantity_visual","summary":"3/4 is bigger than 2/3: 9/12 against 8/12.","quantity_visual":{"kind":"fraction_bars","fractions":[{"numerator":3,"denominator":4},{"numerator":2,"denominator":3}],"steps":[{"label":"Cut both into twelfths","fractions":[{"numerator":9,"denominator":12},{"numerator":8,"denominator":12}]}]}}
quiz: One question with 2-6 options; answerKey stays hidden until they answer, then you hear whether they were right. Example: {"id":"check","type":"quiz","summary":"Where most ATP is made.","quiz":{"question":"Where is most ATP made?","options":[{"id":"nucleus","label":"Nucleus"},{"id":"mito","label":"Mitochondria"}],"answerKey":{"correct":["mito"],"explanation":"The electron chain in the **mitochondria** makes about 34 ATP."}}}
recipe: A dish with ingredients (qty for the servings given; people rescale it) and steps; checkable lets people tick ingredients off together. Example: {"id":"pancakes","type":"recipe","title":"Pancakes","summary":"Pancakes for 4 in 25 minutes.","recipe":{"servings":4,"time":{"prep":10,"cook":15},"ingredients":[{"id":"flour","qty":100,"unit":"g","name":"plain flour"},{"id":"eggs","qty":2,"name":"eggs"}],"steps":[{"id":"mix","text":"Whisk the flour, eggs and milk into a smooth batter."},{"id":"fry","text":"Fry a ladle at a time for a minute each side."}]}}
section: Group of children under the component title. Example: {"id":"s1","type":"section","title":"Your options","children":[…]}
stat_row: 1-4 headline numbers. Example: {"id":"saving","type":"stat_row","summary":"Switching saves £96 a year.","stat_row":{"stats":[{"label":"Yearly saving","value":96,"format":"currency","currency":"GBP","trend":"down","goodDirection":"down"}]}}
steps: 2-10 steps in order; checkable lets people tick them off. Example: {"id":"how","type":"steps","summary":"Three steps to reset the router.","steps":{"items":[{"id":"unplug","title":"Unplug the router"},{"id":"wait","title":"Wait 30 seconds"},{"id":"plug","title":"Plug it back in","detail":"Lights turn green within a minute."}]}}
table: Exact values in rows and columns; each row maps column keys to cells typed by the column kind. Example: {"id":"plans","type":"table","summary":"Two plans by price and data.","table":{"columns":[{"key":"plan","label":"Plan","kind":"text"},{"key":"price","label":"Price","kind":"currency","currency":"GBP"}],"rows":[{"plan":"Basic","price":10},{"plan":"Plus","price":15}]}}
tabs: 2-5 alternative views, e.g. Simple / Detailed. Example: {"id":"t1","type":"tabs","tabs":[{"label":"Simple","children":[…]},{"label":"Detailed","children":[…]}]}
text: Short markdown block (GFM, no HTML). Example: {"id":"lead","type":"text","text":"You use about **half** the data you pay for."}
timeline: 2-20 events in time order; when is the label shown, date (YYYY-MM-DD) only orders. Example: {"id":"history","type":"timeline","summary":"From the Bastille in 1789 to Napoleon in 1799.","timeline":{"events":[{"id":"bastille","when":"1789","title":"Storming of the Bastille"},{"id":"napoleon","when":"1799","title":"Napoleon seizes power"}]}}
